# data/recipe_cache.json is JSON that Atesor writes. A line-by-line git
# merge of it (commit 6b50080) left 35 packages twice, mixed fields of
# neighboring packages and lost 87 packages, so git must not merge it as
# text. Here git stops with a conflict instead.
#
# To merge it by meaning with no conflict, run this once in your clone:
#   sh .github/scripts/setup_git_merge_driver.sh
#
# Without the driver, resolve a conflict by hand (the newest recipe wins):
#   git show :2:data/recipe_cache.json > /tmp/ours.json
#   git show :3:data/recipe_cache.json > /tmp/theirs.json
#   python3 .github/scripts/merge_data_artifacts.py \
#       --merge-caches /tmp/ours.json /tmp/theirs.json \
#       --output data/recipe_cache.json
#   git add data/recipe_cache.json
data/recipe_cache.json merge=binary
